{"id":"000VZN","title":"A Tendency To Lie","author":"The Pi Guy","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-11T06:38:21+00:00","posted":"Heute, 02:30 Uhr","rules":"This week is exactly a year since my first official sudoku, a modifier puzzle inspired by Marty Sears. So what better way to celebrate than another modifier puzzle inspired by Marty Sears. Enjoy. :)\n\nSudoku: Put the digits 1 to 9 once each into every row, column & 3 by 3 box.\n\nLiar Cells: Every row, column & 3 by 3 box contains one liar cell, whose real value is different from its digit.\n\n• Each liar cell contains a different digit from 1 to 9.\n\n• Each liar cell has a different value from 1 to 9.\n\nTen Lines: Each hollow grey line must either contain values adding to 10 or divide into sections that contain values adding to 10.\n\nKropki: Values with a white dot between them must be consecutive. Values with a black dot between them must be such that one digit is double the other.\n\n[The section to the right of the grid is just for keeping track of liar digits & values and is not part of the solution check.]\n\nPuzzle link (SudokuPad)","solutionCode":"The values in column 9 (top to bottom).","tags":["Sudoku","Modifier Cells (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/mhxp6hjg6h","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/mhxp6hjg6h","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":12,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-11T06:38:21+00:00"}